<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Kimberley reports 0.58 carat diamond.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Kimberley reports 0.58 carat diamond.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kimberley Diamond Corp NL said on Tuesday a diamond weighing 0.58 carats was recovered during bulk sample processing of concentrates from the number two pit at its Blina project in Western Australia.</p>
<p>The sphere-like stone, almost white in colour, has some near-surface graphite inclusions but is otherwise of good clarity, the company said.</p>
<p>Last week, Kimberley said a diamond weighing 3.34 carats was recovered from the same pit. So far, 33 diamonds, weighing a total of 11 carats, have been recovered from bulk samples at Blina, the company said.  -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
